  "body_html": "<p>“I’m a Fool to Want You” is a 1951 pop and jazz standard song composed by Frank Sinatra, Jack Wolf, and Joel Herron and first released by Frank Sinatra as a Columbia Records single. The ballad has been covered multiple times by artists in many genre. As a lover of beautiful, sentimental songs about love I picked two of my favorites – the late Bob Dylan and the eternal Billie Holiday.</p>\n<p>With this I’m starting a new fun rubric in the blog – vote for your favorite in comments (I hope it lasts longer:P)!</p>\n<p><img alt=\"late-show-bob-dylan\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-7076\" height=\"515\" src=\"http://www.flowersinagun.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/late-show-bob-dylan.jpg\" width=\"750\"/></p>\n<p><iframe allowfullscreen=\"\" frameborder=\"0\" height=\"248\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/ZLzNANgan7E\" width=\"440\"></iframe></p>\n<p><strong><br/>\nVS </strong></p>\n<p><img alt=\"billie_holiday_downbeat_new_york_n-y-_ca-_feb-_1947_william_p-_gottlieb_04251\" class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-7077\" height=\"900\" src=\"http://www.flowersinagun.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/11/Billie_Holiday_Downbeat_New_York_N.Y._ca._Feb._1947_William_P._Gottlieb_04251.jpg\" width=\"900\"/></p>\n<p><iframe allowfullscreen=\"\" frameborder=\"0\" height=\"248\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/rejizpNR20A\" width=\"440\"></iframe></p>",
